WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.549 --> 00:00:13.219
Hi, welcome back to our at-home retreat.

00:00:13.219 --> 00:00:15.889
And again, thank you Xiaoping for

00:00:15.889 --> 00:00:17.490
translating.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:21.439
This is session number eighteen,

00:00:21.439 --> 00:00:26.260
and we have called it "One Wheel, Two

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:27.550
Lives."

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:30.349
And the picture I chose was a

00:00:30.349 --> 00:00:35.720
human being sort of becoming like a

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:38.470
superhero.

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:44.769
Now, sometimes I use superhero pictures

00:00:44.769 --> 00:00:47.780
to represent a person who's very good

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:58.130
and inspires other people, but in this

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:03.289
drawing we are talking about a human

00:01:03.289 --> 00:01:07.070
being who would like to be reborn in the

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:10.090
deva realm where people look

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:11.970
like superheroes, but then they have

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:22.840
terrible deaths there.

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:23.840
So we've been talking

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:30.590
about sections of the Wheel of Life, and

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:32.990
we kind of felt--it kind of feels to you

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:35.620
doesn't it?--that one Wheel of Life from

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:37.890
one o'clock to twelve o'clock ... that should
be

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:46.790
one lifetime.

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:47.790
But then we learn it's more

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:52.110
complicated than that.

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:53.110
And we saw that

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:55.681
link number eleven, which is rebirth, and
link

00:01:55.681 --> 00:02:05.180
number twelve, which is aging and death,

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:11.510
just two links can be a whole lifetime.

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:13.590
So a very famous question comes up in

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:19.480
the ancient books: how many lifetimes

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:21.590
does it take to get through the whole wheel

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:28.480
one time?

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:29.840
And it's not a just a

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:35.810
philosophical question.

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:36.810
We have to go

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:42.500
through these next two classes ... we have

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:45.430
to talk about how many lifetimes can be

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:52.040
in one wheel, because we're going to find

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:58.770
out something amazing about that wheel.

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:01.880
And that's that if you look at

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:07.260
a Wheel of Life, it's going like this, then

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:14.680
that will trigger another set of links,

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:15.930
and then this one will trigger another

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:19.930
set of links, and then there will be some

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:23.140
links ... three there, three there, three

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:25.569
there, three there ... a few weeks in

00:03:25.569 --> 00:03:35.280
your wheel of life weeks.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:36.280
It can be

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:40.200
triggering many lifetimes, and many

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:44.400
lifetimes can go into one life.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.811
I like to

00:03:46.811 --> 00:03:49.880
think of it like the inside of a fine

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:52.569
watch--a mechanical watch.

00:03:52.569 --> 00:04:01.870
So 
we're going there--we'll talk

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:05.970
about that watch later.

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:06.970
But first let's

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:10.680
just see: how can just two lifetimes fit

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:18.299
in one wheel?

00:04:18.299 --> 00:04:22.000
So let's go to the text and

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:27.020
it says de na hlar kyewa tabu la tsun na
(DES NA LHAR SKYE BA LTA BU LA MTSON NA,)--

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:28.800
let's take the case of a human

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:31.949
being who wants to be born as a deva,

00:04:31.949 --> 00:04:37.210
like a pleasure being.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:40.760
Well, first

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:45.620
we have and then ... de ko na ...
(DE KHO NA ...)

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:47.289
...la mongpay ma rikpa
(...LA RMONGS PA'I MA RIG PA)--

00:04:47.289 --> 00:04:48.289
first you have ... de

00:04:48.289 --> 00:04:52.270
ko na la mongpay ma rikpa means @tattva; you

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:53.669
don't understand @tattva.

00:04:53.669 --> 00:04:55.069
@tattva means "the

00:04:55.069 --> 00:04:59.210
way the world is."

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:02.939
Again, let's go back to

00:05:02.939 --> 00:05:07.759
the kitchen, to the first moment after

00:05:07.759 --> 00:05:13.830
the wife walks in the kitchen.

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:14.830
She

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:17.909
doesn't say anything; she just wants a

00:05:17.909 --> 00:05:18.939
hug.

00:05:18.939 --> 00:05:22.150
And then suddenly her husband blurts out,

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:24.060
"You're so stupid!"

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:27.240
Then what does she say?

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:30.430
[I'm not stupid--you are stupid!]

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.490
No, that's later.

00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:33.509
That's link number two.

00:05:33.509 --> 00:05:34.740
What's number one?

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:36.389
[I didn't do anything!]

00:05:36.389 --> 00:05:40.710
Yeah, "I didn't do anything, and he's yelling
at me!"

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:45.339
Yeah, "I didn't do anything; he yelled at
me!"

00:05:45.339 --> 00:05:47.809
That's link number one.

00:05:47.809 --> 00:05:48.939
It's called

00:05:48.939 --> 00:05:50.439
"misunderstanding."

00:05:50.439 --> 00:05:55.719
She doesn't realize his explosion is

00:05:55.719 --> 00:05:58.349
coming because she yelled at her kids

00:05:58.349 --> 00:06:02.259
last week.

00:06:02.259 --> 00:06:08.159
So, one act of misunderstanding in the

00:06:08.159 --> 00:06:19.729
kitchen, it can throw--project--a whole

00:06:19.729 --> 00:06:25.439
other lifetime, and in the example here,

00:06:25.439 --> 00:06:28.219
marikpay wang gi (MA RIG PA'I DBANG GIS)--that
misunderstanding in

00:06:28.219 --> 00:06:30.279
the kitchen, hlay kyewa pen che kyi kye ne
...

00:06:30.279 --> 00:06:32.300
(LHA'I SKYE BA 'PHEN BYED KYI SKYES NAS ...)

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:37.490
...nyong gyur gyi le (...MYONG 'GYUR GYI LAS)--
it throws... it

00:06:37.490 --> 00:06:41.009
triggers a special kind of karma.

00:06:41.009 --> 00:06:42.759
Now,

00:06:42.759 --> 00:06:50.690
karma can be divided countless ways.

00:06:50.690 --> 00:06:51.690
In

00:06:51.690 --> 00:06:57.819
fact our Mixed Nuts translator group

00:06:57.819 --> 00:07:00.349
is translating several books called

00:07:00.349 --> 00:07:08.099
all the many ways you can divide karma.

00:07:08.099 --> 00:07:13.000
But, there's a very famous division into

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:17.740
three kinds of karma.

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:19.180
Number one: tong...

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:20.180
(MTHONG...)

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:23.969
...gyur kyi le (...'GYUR GYI LAS)--means karma

00:07:23.969 --> 00:07:26.340
which is so powerful that you will see

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:29.659
the result in this life before you die.

00:07:29.659 --> 00:07:40.050
Second: kye ne nyong gyur gyi le
(SKYES NAS MYONG 'GYUR GYI LAS)--karma

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:49.199
which will create your very next life.

00:07:49.199 --> 00:07:53.149
Then what's called shen la nyong gyur gyi
le (GZHAN LA MYONG 'GYUR GYI LAS)

00:07:53.149 --> 00:07:56.439
means karma which will create all or

00:07:56.439 --> 00:08:07.849
many lives after the next life.

00:08:07.849 --> 00:08:09.669
So in this case, the book is talking...

00:08:09.669 --> 00:08:11.969
the lam rim (LAM RIM) book is talking about
kye ne

00:08:11.969 --> 00:08:14.429
nyong gyur gyi le--you're going to ... you're

00:08:14.429 --> 00:08:17.849
creating karma which will throw your

00:08:17.849 --> 00:08:22.699
very next life.

00:08:22.699 --> 00:08:29.939
And the example here is a

00:08:29.939 --> 00:08:37.750
life as a deva or a pleasure being.

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:38.750
Now I

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:43.260
have to change my story, okay?

00:08:43.260 --> 00:08:44.260
Because you

00:08:44.260 --> 00:08:47.139
cannot be born as a pleasure being from

00:08:47.139 --> 00:08:52.990
yelling at your husband.

00:08:52.990 --> 00:08:54.810
So she must have

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:57.339
come in the kitchen and said, "Honey,

00:08:57.339 --> 00:08:59.279
you're the most special person in my

00:08:59.279 --> 00:09:10.500
life," because he gave her a big hug.

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:12.830
But

00:09:12.830 --> 00:09:16.370
actually, she should say, "I didn't do

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:21.209
anything and he gave me a hug?"

00:09:21.209 --> 00:09:22.209
So she ...

00:09:22.209 --> 00:09:25.000
she doesn't understand.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.089
The hug she got

00:09:26.089 --> 00:09:28.860
from her husband is coming from hugging

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:35.029
her kids last week.

00:09:35.029 --> 00:09:36.029
So she's saying

00:09:36.029 --> 00:09:38.150
something nice, "Oh, I love you!

00:09:38.150 --> 00:09:39.150
Thank you

00:09:39.150 --> 00:09:45.940
for the hug, honey!"

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:47.620
But still she's saying it

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:50.030
because of link number one: she doesn't

00:09:50.030 --> 00:09:58.090
really understand.

00:09:58.090 --> 00:10:00.930
So without understanding the hug came

00:10:00.930 --> 00:10:03.250
from a seed in her mind from giving

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:11.649
her kids a hug last week, she reacts in a

00:10:11.649 --> 00:10:17.529
positive way and says, "I love you, honey.

00:10:17.529 --> 00:10:21.329
Thank you!"

00:10:21.329 --> 00:10:26.980
And she plants a new seed.

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:28.519
Where?

00:10:28.519 --> 00:10:31.600
Fifty dollars.

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:32.600
More exact.

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:33.600
Where?

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:37.000
Where does she plant

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:39.269
the seed?

00:10:39.269 --> 00:10:40.399
Tim?

00:10:40.399 --> 00:10:41.540
No.

00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:43.259
She plants the seed on the

00:10:43.259 --> 00:10:47.720
first half of link number three.

00:10:47.720 --> 00:10:50.490
Okay?

00:10:50.490 --> 00:10:54.910
That's where she plants her seed.

00:10:54.910 --> 00:10:57.320
Then der kye na chi marung nyam du mon lam...

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:58.800
(DER SKYES NA CI MA RUNG SNYAM DU SMON LAM...)

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:00.570
...sok kyi dunpa chepa ni
(...SOGS KYIS 'DUN PA BYED PA NI)--

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:01.610
and then later

00:11:01.610 --> 00:11:03.160
she says, "Wow!

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:04.470
I made some good karma--I

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:11.560
was nice to my husband.

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:12.709
I pray that good

00:11:12.709 --> 00:11:15.430
karma will make me a deva in my next

00:11:15.430 --> 00:11:17.720
life."

00:11:17.720 --> 00:11:26.720
And in this example, that's arming

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:28.959
the karma at link number eight.

00:11:28.959 --> 00:11:29.959
It's like the

00:11:29.959 --> 00:11:35.300
water on the seed.

00:11:35.300 --> 00:11:40.699
dunpa de nyi che ru...

00:11:40.699 --> 00:11:41.839
('DUN PA DE NYID CHE RU...)

00:11:41.839 --> 00:11:44.480
...tsunpa ni (...BRTZON PA NI)--
and then if she feels that wish

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:50.389
more and more, it becomes almost like

00:11:50.389 --> 00:11:52.389
obsession with her, "Oh, that good karma

00:11:52.389 --> 00:11:55.190
should make me a pleasure being in my

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:59.540
next life."

00:11:59.540 --> 00:12:05.050
Then she's putting fertilizer--link

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:12.790
number nine--on that karma, also.

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:15.050
And

00:12:15.050 --> 00:12:18.329
because of those two--water and

00:12:18.329 --> 00:12:24.110
fertilizer--the karma that she planted in

00:12:24.110 --> 00:12:30.670
the kitchen at link number two, it becomes
a

00:12:30.670 --> 00:12:36.410
very, very powerful, fat seed ready to

00:12:36.410 --> 00:12:42.089
break open.

00:12:42.089 --> 00:12:45.050
And we call it... here it says

00:12:45.050 --> 00:12:47.339
chi kar ('CHI KHAR)--in the moment of her
death,

00:12:47.339 --> 00:12:48.860
right, in the last moment of her

00:12:48.860 --> 00:13:00.170
awareness 
of this world, those wishes to

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:06.319
go to a certain future, they make the

00:13:06.319 --> 00:13:14.180
good karma seed fat. de nyi pen nge su chepay
le

00:13:14.180 --> 00:13:15.180
(DE NYID 'PHEN NGES SU BYAS PA'I LAS)--

00:13:15.180 --> 00:13:18.269
and that seed becomes definite: it will

00:13:18.269 --> 00:13:23.220
open into a pleasure being's rebirth.

00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:26.480
So,

00:13:26.480 --> 00:13:37.100
our author summarizes: if you think about

00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:47.040
it, we've had like two and a half thrower...

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:48.139
throwers?

00:13:48.139 --> 00:13:49.240
Archers.

00:13:49.240 --> 00:13:52.500
Two and a half.

00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:53.579
Number

00:13:53.579 --> 00:13:58.819
one, she misunderstood her husband.

00:13:58.819 --> 00:13:59.819
Number

00:13:59.819 --> 00:14:02.660
two, but she gave him a very beautiful

00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:06.660
hug.

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:10.199
Number three, in that moment she

00:14:10.199 --> 00:14:14.860
imprinted a seed on her mind.

00:14:14.860 --> 00:14:17.001
Now, so

00:14:17.001 --> 00:14:21.790
that's kind of three links, and then

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:26.829
three more links are like the factory.

00:14:26.829 --> 00:14:28.999
she misunderstands...

00:14:28.999 --> 00:14:33.850
well let's say she has a feelings about

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:37.579
the seed, really.

00:14:37.579 --> 00:14:38.579
She wants them...

00:14:38.579 --> 00:14:39.579
she's

00:14:39.579 --> 00:14:41.070
doing like coffee meditation where that

00:14:41.070 --> 00:14:47.220
seed should open.

00:14:47.220 --> 00:14:48.220
First coffee

00:14:48.220 --> 00:14:51.509
meditation, stronger meditation--coffee

00:14:51.509 --> 00:14:54.999
meditation, and then the seed is fat and

00:14:54.999 --> 00:14:59.810
ready to open.

00:14:59.810 --> 00:15:04.870
Those six links--three

00:15:04.870 --> 00:15:10.740
archer links, three links which make the

00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:18.360
seed ready to explode--those six of the

00:15:18.360 --> 00:15:21.800
twelve links are happening in the first

00:15:21.800 --> 00:15:22.800
life.

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:30.930
de ne chi mar hlar kye
DE NAS PHYI MAR LHAR SKYE)--and then that

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:31.930
seed

00:15:31.930 --> 00:15:38.730
breaks open and she goes into a new life,

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:44.290
and she becomes that pleasure being, deva.

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:53.809
We call it deva or temporary pleasure life.

00:15:53.809 --> 00:15:58.319
It can last for a million years, and it's

00:15:58.319 --> 00:16:00.309
very, very pleasant and you look like

00:16:00.309 --> 00:16:11.449
Iron Man or Superwoman, or something.

00:16:11.449 --> 00:16:15.120
But when you die,

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:18.180
you always go to hell.

00:16:18.180 --> 00:16:20.370
"Oh, why?"

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:21.370
You burned

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:24.309
up all your good karma.

00:16:24.309 --> 00:16:25.309
So we think it's

00:16:25.309 --> 00:16:28.259
like something you should avoid--that

00:16:28.259 --> 00:16:31.890
kind of deva rebirth.

00:16:31.890 --> 00:16:35.290
They are just

00:16:35.290 --> 00:16:39.420
having fun, they don't try to improve

00:16:39.420 --> 00:16:45.480
themselves, they don't learn more, they

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:49.470
kill their old good karma.

00:16:49.470 --> 00:16:50.759
It's like very

00:16:50.759 --> 00:16:54.740
wealthy children in this world.

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:58.910
Oftentimes, they they spend their whole

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:02.899
life using money without working.

00:17:02.899 --> 00:17:04.709
chi mar...

00:17:04.709 --> 00:17:06.520
(PHYI MAR...)

00:17:06.520 --> 00:17:13.540
...hlar kyewa na (...LHAR SKYE BA NA)--so
let's say she's

00:17:13.540 --> 00:17:20.210
reborn like she wished.

00:17:20.210 --> 00:17:22.550
So what links are going to happen in the

00:17:22.550 --> 00:17:28.330
second life?

00:17:28.330 --> 00:17:29.620
ming suk (MING GZUGS)--to the body and

00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:32.270
mind entering the mom's womb.

00:17:32.270 --> 00:17:33.270
Number four,

00:17:33.270 --> 00:17:36.430
link number four--the body and mind entering

00:17:36.430 --> 00:17:41.080
the mother's womb.

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:44.030
Then link number five, her

00:17:44.030 --> 00:17:50.330
ears, eyes, nose--they are forming.

00:17:50.330 --> 00:17:51.330
Link

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:54.880
0
number six, because of those sense organs,

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:56.510
she will make contact with the outside

00:17:56.510 --> 00:17:58.070
world.

00:17:58.070 --> 00:18:04.370
Then automatically, link number seven--

00:18:04.370 --> 00:18:05.930
she will start to have pleasant

00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:07.770
experiences and she will start to have

00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:13.140
unpleasant experiences.

00:18:13.140 --> 00:18:15.400
And four, five, six,

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:21.810
seven--those four links and you can kind

00:18:21.810 --> 00:18:32.830
of throw in half of her link number three,
too (conscousness)--

00:18:32.830 --> 00:18:37.000
they are going to turn into kyewa (SKYE BA)
and...

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:39.400
...ga shi (...RGA SHI)--they're going to turn
into link eleven

00:18:39.400 --> 00:18:44.020
and link twelve.

00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:47.920
They are a whole life--

00:18:47.920 --> 00:18:52.070
those four, or maybe five.

00:18:52.070 --> 00:18:54.680
Yeah, and the

00:18:54.680 --> 00:18:58.190
whole life is the two links: birth, and

00:18:58.190 --> 00:19:01.650
aging and death.

00:19:01.650 --> 00:19:09.320
Okay, so we have six resulting links.

00:19:09.320 --> 00:19:16.650
chi ma hlay ten de la dzokpa te
(PHYI MA LHA'I RTEN DE LA RDZOGS PA STE,)

00:19:16.650 --> 00:19:18.970
those six links are finished in the

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:23.000
deva birth.

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:26.680
So, we had six links in the

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:30.250
first life as a human, and six links in

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:36.470
the second life as a deva.

00:19:36.470 --> 00:19:42.050
And this is

00:19:42.050 --> 00:19:45.490
the way in which two lifetimes can be

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:52.680
finished in one wheel.

00:19:52.680 --> 00:19:58.290
But I ask you to think about something.

00:19:58.290 --> 00:20:08.030
And this is a little deeper.

00:20:08.030 --> 00:20:09.030
Is it

00:20:09.030 --> 00:20:11.900
possible that the karma she plants in

00:20:11.900 --> 00:20:17.830
one life is not watered for a few more

00:20:17.830 --> 00:20:22.130
lives--like the seed is just sitting there
...

00:20:22.130 --> 00:20:27.990
Is it possible you could plant a seed today
and it will

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:30.250
take three lifetimes before that seed

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:37.800
gets watered?

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:38.960
Is it possible to plant a

00:20:38.960 --> 00:20:43.450
seed today or have a seed... there's a seed

00:20:43.450 --> 00:20:52.820
in Siberia, in Russia--it's a special flower.

00:20:52.820 --> 00:20:55.580
They found one in the ice, which has been

00:20:55.580 --> 00:21:05.510
there for thirty-one thousand years.

00:21:05.510 --> 00:21:06.510
And

00:21:06.510 --> 00:21:10.060
they planted it, and they put water on it,

00:21:10.060 --> 00:21:12.200
and it grew a flower after thirty-one

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:18.020
thousand years.

00:21:18.020 --> 00:21:19.210
So is it possible that

00:21:19.210 --> 00:21:29.560
it might take more wheels before it opens?

00:21:29.560 --> 00:21:32.010
We have to think about it.

00:21:32.010 --> 00:21:33.010
But in today's

00:21:33.010 --> 00:21:39.030
example, six links in the first life, six

00:21:39.030 --> 00:21:42.800
links in the second life--twelve links in

00:21:42.800 --> 00:21:45.750
two lifes.

00:21:45.750 --> 00:21:48.630
Now there's a special

00:21:48.630 --> 00:21:50.280
expression in Tibetan that you should

00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:51.860
know, if you want to go deeper.

00:21:51.860 --> 00:21:57.380
By the way, if you don't want to go

00:21:57.380 --> 00:22:01.390
deeper, go get a pam she (SPAM BSHAD), pam
she.

00:22:01.390 --> 00:22:06.280
It's a special Tibetan word called pam

00:22:06.280 --> 00:22:07.750
she.

00:22:07.750 --> 00:22:12.450
pam she means go find a teacher

00:22:12.450 --> 00:22:17.500
who didn't have much training, and

00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:21.610
they'll say, "You know, be nice!"

00:22:21.610 --> 00:22:24.570
"You know,

00:22:24.570 --> 00:22:28.850
do it... do your @manis--@om mani padme hum--and

00:22:28.850 --> 00:22:32.360
everything will be okay."

00:22:32.360 --> 00:22:33.360
If that's enough

00:22:33.360 --> 00:22:39.490
for you, then you don't need this lam rim,
okay?

00:22:39.490 --> 00:22:42.830
But, I'm trying to get you to understand the

00:22:42.830 --> 00:22:48.940
inside of the clock.

00:22:48.940 --> 00:22:49.940
How does each piece

00:22:49.940 --> 00:22:53.600
work?

00:22:53.600 --> 00:22:56.960
Because to change that clock--@mar...

00:22:56.960 --> 00:22:59.360
...mahatha...

00:22:59.360 --> 00:23:00.420
for $50.

00:23:00.420 --> 00:23:02.450
[killing point] Yeah!

00:23:02.450 --> 00:23:04.650
You have to know the strike

00:23:04.650 --> 00:23:08.550
point.

00:23:08.550 --> 00:23:10.470
If you want to--it's a terrible

00:23:10.470 --> 00:23:12.570
example, but it's in the scripture--if you

00:23:12.570 --> 00:23:20.830
want to kill a human in two seconds, like

00:23:20.830 --> 00:23:29.330
those kung fu masters, cut this vein right
here and the person has

00:23:29.330 --> 00:23:30.330
to die.

00:23:30.330 --> 00:23:31.670
You cannot fix it.

00:23:31.670 --> 00:23:32.760
They have

00:23:32.760 --> 00:23:34.750
to die in two minutes.

00:23:34.750 --> 00:23:37.981
I have a friend, he

00:23:37.981 --> 00:23:43.220
was building a house, he fell down, then a

00:23:43.220 --> 00:23:50.730
nail scratched him here.

00:23:50.730 --> 00:23:53.040
And he was standing

00:23:53.040 --> 00:23:57.040
next to his wife,

00:23:57.040 --> 00:24:00.780
and he died in two minutes.

00:24:00.780 --> 00:24:02.231
And she's... she

00:24:02.231 --> 00:24:04.450
couldn't do anything.

00:24:04.450 --> 00:24:06.840
Okay, so... we want to

00:24:06.840 --> 00:24:11.330
kill the wheel, so you have to understand

00:24:11.330 --> 00:24:18.390
the anatomy of @sansara.

00:24:18.390 --> 00:24:19.390
And where's the

00:24:19.390 --> 00:24:22.620
exact place you have to cut... cut your

00:24:22.620 --> 00:24:27.350
suffering?

00:24:27.350 --> 00:24:28.370
So that's why we're doing all

00:24:28.370 --> 00:24:34.010
this detail, okay?

00:24:34.010 --> 00:24:35.250
So anyway, that word I

00:24:35.250 --> 00:24:41.820
wanted to say tendrel tsar chik
(RTEN 'BREL TSAR GCIG)--it

00:24:41.820 --> 00:24:49.380
means one time through the twelve... one

00:24:49.380 --> 00:24:52.670
time through the twelve.

00:24:52.670 --> 00:24:56.400
I didn't say "wheel."

00:24:56.400 --> 00:25:00.600
I said one time through the twelve--we

00:25:00.600 --> 00:25:05.410
don't know which twelve, and we'll talk more

00:25:05.410 --> 00:25:11.809
about it.

00:25:11.809 --> 00:25:13.810
We'll talk about it later.

00:25:13.810 --> 00:25:15.580
Okay, last thing today.

00:25:15.580 --> 00:25:19.040
ngen dro tabur tsun na
(NGAN 'GRO LTA BUR MTSON NA,)--

00:25:19.040 --> 00:25:21.510
Okay that was with taking a good

00:25:21.510 --> 00:25:24.250
rebirth.

00:25:24.250 --> 00:25:26.990
So let's talk about a bad

00:25:26.990 --> 00:25:27.990
rebirth.

00:25:27.990 --> 00:25:33.070
We call... ngen dro (NGAN 'GRO) means "lower

00:25:33.070 --> 00:25:37.340
realms"--three kinds: animal, hungry ghost,
hell.

00:25:37.340 --> 00:25:38.770
okay tabur...

00:25:38.770 --> 00:25:41.990
Now he says, "Let's talk about

00:25:41.990 --> 00:25:43.590
a bad rebirth."

00:25:43.590 --> 00:25:47.410
lendre la mongpa marikpa
(LAS 'BRAS LA RMONGS PA'I MA RIG PA)--

00:25:47.410 --> 00:25:50.090
again it starts with misunderstanding

00:25:50.090 --> 00:25:56.080
how karma works.

00:25:56.080 --> 00:25:57.950
But in a deeper misunderstanding where

00:25:57.950 --> 00:26:04.920
you just say, "I don't believe it at all."

00:26:04.920 --> 00:26:05.920
Then you

00:26:05.920 --> 00:26:07.060
don't feel like you have to do good

00:26:07.060 --> 00:26:08.760
things to other people; you can just do

00:26:08.760 --> 00:26:13.410
bad things.

00:26:13.410 --> 00:26:14.840
So if your misunderstanding

00:26:14.840 --> 00:26:21.660
is that bad, you will kill people, you

00:26:21.660 --> 00:26:25.010
will lie to people, and you will collect

00:26:25.010 --> 00:26:29.670
sok (GSOG) means you will "collect" bad karma.

00:26:29.670 --> 00:26:32.640
Then that has its own water, its own

00:26:32.640 --> 00:26:34.950
fertilizer, in your mind.

00:26:34.950 --> 00:26:41.350
gong gi rik dre
(GONG GIS RIGS 'GRE)

00:26:41.350 --> 00:26:43.660
means "Hey, and the rest is the same as I

00:26:43.660 --> 00:26:51.530
told you before with the good karma."

00:26:51.530 --> 00:26:52.530
And

00:26:52.530 --> 00:26:56.720
that completes session eighteen.

00:26:56.720 --> 00:26:57.720
Tomorrow we're

00:26:57.720 --> 00:27:01.700
going on to can you have three lifetimes

00:27:01.700 --> 00:27:08.750
in twelve links?

00:27:08.750 --> 00:27:09.810
Can you finish a set of

00:27:09.810 --> 00:27:15.361
twelve in three different wheels, almost--

00:27:15.361 --> 00:27:23.130
three different lifetimes?

00:27:23.130 --> 00:27:24.130
And we'll talk

00:27:24.130 --> 00:27:27.240
about that one tomorrow.

00:27:27.240 --> 00:27:30.820
Don't turn your mind off, you know.

00:27:30.820 --> 00:27:34.230
Don't say, "This is too complicated!" okay?

00:27:34.230 --> 00:27:39.920
You went through twelve years or sixteen years
of

00:27:39.920 --> 00:27:42.330
school.

00:27:42.330 --> 00:27:43.480
At the end, you could do very

00:27:43.480 --> 00:27:49.000
complicated mathematics, and very

00:27:49.000 --> 00:27:52.880
complicated science, and maybe you could

00:27:52.880 --> 00:27:55.650
write complicated things from your

00:27:55.650 --> 00:28:00.190
language classes.

00:28:00.190 --> 00:28:02.630
But nobody taught you how to die.

00:28:02.630 --> 00:28:04.950
Now you

00:28:04.950 --> 00:28:08.310
don't... you may not be a mathematician in

00:28:08.310 --> 00:28:13.410
your life, you may not write books or be

00:28:13.410 --> 00:28:19.150
a scientist--and that happens to a lot of

00:28:19.150 --> 00:28:21.110
us--and that means you didn't need those

00:28:21.110 --> 00:28:26.780
twelve years.

00:28:26.780 --> 00:28:28.100
But to spend a few days

00:28:28.100 --> 00:28:34.320
learning how to die, which you have to do,

00:28:34.320 --> 00:28:38.410
I think it makes sense, okay?

00:28:38.410 --> 00:28:39.410
So see you

00:28:39.410 --> 00:28:40.410
at class nineteen.

00:28:40.410 --> 00:28:43.190
Thank you, and thanks Xiaoping

00:28:43.190 --> 00:28:52.630
for translating.

